5. DEFECT F1 (blocking, routed to Green)

file: apps/www-reading-advantage/src/lib/tutor-commission.ts:96 (toSatang)
Failing test: apps/www-reading-advantage/src/lib/tutor-commission.adversarial.test.ts > A6 finite
input whose product overflows > a finite price whose volume overflows returns finite money instead of
throwing.

Exact failure:
  RangeError: The number Infinity cannot be converted to a BigInt because it is not an integer
  at toSatang src/lib/tutor-commission.ts:96
  via flatSatang src/lib/tutor-commission.ts:106
  via calculateNetwork src/lib/tutor-commission.ts:171

Probe inputs that throw:
  {price: 1e307, personalStudents: 1}
  {price: 1e306, personalStudents: 1000}
  {price: 1e306, studentsPerLeg: [1000]}
  {price: Number.MAX_VALUE}

Cause: a finite price times a finite count overflows to Infinity. toSatang calls BigInt(Infinity).
The component price input has no max (tutor-commission-calculator.tsx:221). readNumber
(tutor-commission-calculator.tsx:94) clamps only non-finite typed text. A typed 1e307 reaches
calculateNetwork during render, so the calculator throws instead of showing a figure.

Spec basis: spec 5.2 module rule 1 says a non-finite input becomes 0. Strategy 4.2 requires every
attack case to return finite, non-negative money.

Smallest fix:
  - line 148: const ownVolume = clampNonNegative(price * personalStudents);
  - line 152: const volume = clampNonNegative(price * students);
  - line 169: const networkVolume = clampNonNegative(ownVolume + legVolume);
  - toSatang head: if (!Number.isFinite(baht)) return 0n;
No normal input changes value. The four probe inputs then return zero money, and the satang
conservation helper holds.

Severity is low. The input range is extreme. F1 blocks only because the gate holds a red test.
If the PM judges a class price above 1e306 out of contract, the PM may waive F1. The one red case
then moves to a known residual.

6. NONBLOCKING NOTES

N1 (info) tutor-commission.ts:57. The NetworkResult.preTax JSDoc says "not displayed". The payout
graph renders preTax as the chart.you row (tutor-commission-calculator.tsx:345). Spec D-9 item 2
requires the graph rows to sum to the gross. The row is correct. Only the doc sentence is stale.
No fix is required in this phase.

N2 (info) tutor-commission.ts:179. Above 2^53 satang the baht Number return cannot carry every
satang. At 1e15 baht with one leg the integer path is exact (71428571200642857 satang). The
returned Numbers recover 71428571200642860, 16 satang off. This is the Number return contract, not
the integer rule. The exact pins live at 1e9 with a leg and at 1e15 own-only, where every value is
a multiple of 16 and recovers exactly.

